{
  "name": "lynx",
  "_about": "the Eurasian lynx SCULPTED on the cat frame (2026-11-06, gen: scratchpad sc/m5/lynx.py from the tiger's shapes): a metre head-body and 65 cm at the shoulder -- short in the body and high on long legs, the hindquarters above the shoulders; big round furred paws; a short bobbed tail with a black tip; a small round head framed by a ruff of pale fur down the jaw line to points beside the throat, a thin dark line along each cheek, tall pointed black-backed ears each with a long black tuft; sandy-grey to reddish, spotted small to medium (coats: grey, red, heavily spotted), white beneath. Shy and solitary: one at the forest's edge (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): tall pointed cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`), the edge black on both faces (a pale patch in the black back), the hollow pale; the long black tuft the outline run on past the tip as a narrow spike (black by the edge band); the roots faired. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 12 ivory whiskers a side, 4 rows on the whisker pad (56-84 mm); 3 ivory whiskers a side, a brow tuft (27-36 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh). (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/tails.py) The TAIL is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along its bones, not a chain of cones blended one into the next: no beads, its thin end exact rings.",
